6. Covenants

    6.1 Borrower Covenants
    - To pay the Lender the principal sum of [LOAN AMOUNT] on the Maturity Date and any other amounts due under this Agreement on or before the respective due dates.
    - To pay the Lender the interest on the outstanding principal balance at the rate of [INTEREST RATE] per annum, calculated on the actual number of days elapsed, and to make quarterly installments of principal and interest on the respective due dates.
    - To maintain the property securing this Agreement in good condition, ordinary wear and tear excepted, and to keep the property insured against loss or damage by fire and other perils.
    - To keep the Lender fully informed of the financial condition of the Borrower and of the use of the proceeds of this loan.
    - To grant the Lender such access to the property as may be necessary to inspect the property and the books and records of the Borrower relating to the property.

    6.2 Lender Covenants
    - To advance the principal sum of [LOAN AMOUNT] to the Borrower in accordance with the terms of this Agreement.
    - To apply the proceeds of this loan solely for the purpose of [LOAN PURPOSE].
    - To not, without the prior written consent of the Borrower, release or otherwise discharge any of the security for this loan, except in the ordinary course of business.
    - To not, without the prior written consent of the Borrower, waive or modify any of the terms or conditions of this Agreement.

7. Conditions Precedent
TEXT:

Lender's obligation to advance the loan is subject to the following conditions precedent:

- Approval of this Agreement by the Lender's board of directors or other duly authorized committee.
- Receipt by the Lender of satisfactory evidence that the Borrower has obtained any necessary permits, licenses, or approvals for the purpose of [LOAN PURPOSE].
- Receipt by the Lender of a satisfactory title search or other evidence of the Borrower's ownership or right to possession of the property securing this loan.
- Receipt by the Lender of a satisfactory environmental report regarding the property securing this loan.
- Receipt by the Lender of the original or duly certified copies of all documents necessary to perfect the Lender's security interest in the property securing this loan.
- The Borrower's execution and delivery of this Agreement on or before the Loan Date.
- The Borrower's payment of all fees and expenses incurred by the Lender in connection with this loan.
- The Borrower's compliance with all applicable laws and regulations in connection with this loan and the use of the proceeds of this loan.
- The Borrower's representation and warranty that the Borrower has full authority to enter into this Agreement and to grant the security for this loan.

Upon the satisfaction of the conditions precedent, the Lender shall have the right to disburse the loan to the Borrower.

